# Website copy

Rules for copy, UI text, titles, meta descriptions, and comments on this site.

## No em dashes

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`).

Prefer commas, periods, colons, parentheses, or a rewritten sentence.

## No “X is Y, not Z”

Do not define the product or the practice by what it is not.

Do not write “this, not that,” “a journal, not a chatbot,” or similar contrast.

Say what happens instead: you write a fragment. It saves. You get a short reflection. You walk away.

Bad: `Journal42 is a journal, not a chatbot.`

Good: `Journal42 is a private journal. You write a fragment and walk away.`

## Voice

Short sentences. Named hours (kids asleep, Slack open, the review still playing).

If you need medical or crisis care, use those services. This is a private journal. Write that as its own sentences. Do not frame it as a contrast.
